# Recoverable Insight Nexus repair archives

These archives preserve local Git history while active-writer coordination is pending. **They are not integrated or tested product source. Nothing has been pushed or deployed.** This backup branch retains PR #3 source at 3a4bd4de5e531140fc827a8ea3106092bf748681 and adds archive/documentation files only.

- `retained-history.bundle`: all retained repair history ending at d5de90df667ecb3cef9c237f2d332847e154b54a, including cfb2165, 0b23727, 503b43b, f1143b5 and earlier provider/image/ownership fixes and evidence.
- `stopped-port.bundle`: the canonical repository history plus incomplete isolated port checkpoint d253b2fff08828c52e42d4dac8a91b7d745b6883, based on PR #3 head. Its checked-in checklist identifies missing work and active writer. Do not publish it as a completed repair.
- `manifest.json`: archive SHA-256, byte counts, source heads and validation scope. A limited credential-shaped literal/service-role JWT scan found no matches; it is not a guarantee about every possible sensitive datum.

Both bundles passed `git bundle verify`, were cloned without network into fresh allowed temporary directories, and passed `git fsck --full`. Restored HEADs equal the source heads above. This proves archive recoverability, not source behavior or live acceptance.

The original source task “Analyze and deploy with Cloudflare” is not loaded. A different active writer, “Review tracking and scraping code” (01a19442-d436-70e0-a691-65869f46164f), is integrating Intelligence Lab, migration and Cloudflare packaging in D:/CodexProjects/github-merge-verification-2026-10-17/repos/NexusInsights__dark-trace-loom. Its task registry cwd is not assumed to identify that repository. Do not apply/push intersecting repair code before agreeing the canonical checkpoint and ownership.

Explicit human permission to send that coordination message is pending under the thread tool's direct-authorization rule. Source editing stopped when the active writer was identified. No denied source-access retry followed; the newly authorized three-file owner hash read succeeded once.

